{title: Leaning on the Everlasting Arms}
{artist: Elisha A. Hoffman / Anthony J. Showalter}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 405장}
{title_ko: 주의 친절한 팔에 안기세}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
What a [G]fellowship, what a [C]joy di[G]vine
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
What a [G]blessedness, what a [C]peace is [G]mine
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Leaning, leaning, [C]safe and se[G]cure from all alarms
[G]Leaning, leaning, [C]leaning on the [G]ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh, how [G]sweet to walk in this [C]pilgrim [G]way
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
Oh, how [G]bright the path grows from [C]day to [G]day
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
What have [G]I to dread, what have [C]I to [G]fear
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
I have [G]blessed peace with my [C]Lord so [G]near
Leaning [G]on the ever[D7]lasting [G]arms
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
